From c5e36360799056fd3fa41e299a142c68c3047c56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mat Kowalski <mko@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 15:04:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] CNO: typed VIPManagement access and runtimecfg-aligned
 peer schema

The vendored configv1 now carries BareMetalPlatformStatus.VIPManagement,
so drop the unstructured live GET in favor of the bootstrap result, and
gate rendering on the BGPBasedVIPManagement feature gate. The
bgp-vip-config schema follows the installer rename to defaultPeers with
flat hostOverrides (matching baremetal-runtimecfg's FRRPeerMapping).
---
 pkg/network/bgp_vip.go      | 62 ++++++++++++-------------------------
 pkg/network/bgp_vip_test.go | 30 ++++++++++++++++++
 pkg/network/render.go       |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 50 insertions(+), 44 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 pkg/network/bgp_vip_test.go

diff --git a/pkg/network/bgp_vip.go b/pkg/network/bgp_vip.go
